This guy has the chance of a snowball in hell against any 
shopkeeper.  The first thing you should do is:  Try to 
sell items until you can pay the debt.  If it's a food 
store, this won't work, otherwise you can get off the 
hook this way.  (Don't worry, your pets can steal the 
stuff back later.)  If you have the bad luck of being 
in a food store, your only chance is escape.  The best 
thing to do is zapping a wand of digging downwards and 
avoiding this level for quite some time.  The next-best 
thing is to read a scroll of teleportation while being 
confused, which will make you level-teleport, or to quaff 
a cursed potion of gain level, which raises you up the ceiling.  
The third option is to read a teleport scroll without being 
confused, and run like hell towards the stairs.  The fourth 
and least desirable option is to somehow escape/fight the 
shopkeeper per pedes.  Some ideas (use at your own risk!):  

- It seems best to me to kick the door first, then 
  take care of the shopkeeper.  He will have a round 
  of attack at you this way, but you can dive behind 
  him in the tunnel and don't have to waste time to 
  kick the door open or maneuver around him to get 
  through the doorway while he's angry.  

- Any means of slowing/hindering him are _good_.  
  He's very fast and I assume that he will follow 
  you up/downstairs, so you have to slow him down.  
  Anyway, if you don't, you'll be dead long before 
  you reach the stairs.  Wands of sleep, potions of 
  paralysis (wielding is better than throwing, I think), 
  scrolls of earth (cursed preferred) and maybe even 
  wands of slow monster can save your day.  

- If you really, really want or have to fight him, 
  dont' do the door-kick first, but instead start 
  with ranged attacks.  Prefer cold attacks, since 
  this might shatter his healing potions (he usually 
  has some).  Try to overwhelm him while he's still 
  zapping his wand of striking (usually his first 
  choice[1]).  
 
- I don't know exactly if the kops will appear if 
  you leave the shop while already being attacked 
  by the shopkeeper.  If so, they carry cream pies, 
  and though they might blind you, you can also turn 
  the table around and blind the shopkeeper with them.  
  Try to get the kops between you and the shopkeeper 
  somehow, they're much less powerful.  

